:local {
  .InMapOverlaycontrols {
    // Because of the lovely Sticky component that calculates the height of the header and the component,
    // a race condition is introduced. Because of that I noticed that the map controls are sometimes
    // rendered as if they had bottom set to 0. That is because the sticky rendered the next frame after the absolute positioning
    // was calculated, meaning that in order for the absolute positioning to be recalculated correctly, a resize event has to be triggered.
    // Since the controls are positioned at the bottom of the screen, the easiest solution is to position them as fixed. The second fix would be
    // to rewrite the Sticky component and make it sticky in CSS.
    position: fixed;
    bottom: 1.25rem;
    right: 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    transition: bottom 0.25s ease-in-out;
  }
}
